  "summary": "User James O'Connor (user_id 8, Warehouse Supervisor, Operations, usual hours 06:00-14:00 Central) reports two issues: (1) his desktop BL-DT-0108 has no network connection, and (2) floor 2 printer BL-PR-FL2 is down. Checked: account is active, not sign-in blocked, 0 failed logins, VPN access enabled, must_change_password false. Triage flagged user_blocked=true, but the account lookup shows sign_in_blocked=false, so please verify. BL-DT-0108: online=false, last check-in 2026-10-11 01:34 UTC, no warnings, disk 78% free. BL-PR-FL2: online=false, last check-in 2026-10-10 22:34 UTC, no warnings, assigned to nobody. Per KB-022 this means the printer itself is the problem for everyone, not just this user. KB-022 needs someone on site to read the printer screen and power-cycle it, and I could not do that. No KB article covers a wired desktop with no network (KB-014 is Wi-Fi with internet access, which does not match). Needed: on-site check of the desktop's network cable and port/switch, and of the floor 2 printer's screen, power, and network link. Also check whether the printer and desktop share the same network segment or switch, since both are offline.",
  "reason": "Desktop has no network connectivity with no matching KB article, and the floor 2 printer is offline and needs on-site hardware or network checks. Both are P2 and outside Tier 1 tools."
}
